// BUG-ZYB-008 / MM-12 — module state read through a function that does not
// name it.
//
// A write to module state reached the store only when the frame that made it
// returned. Until then it was visible to that frame, and to whatever it called
// *directly* — because the injection looks for a live copy in the caller's own
// scope before falling back to the store. One function in between, one that
// does not mention the variable and so has none of it injected, and the call
// after that read the store, which had not heard about the write yet.
//
// This is the whole of it:
//
//     correr()  { v = "nuevo"  _lee()  _medio() }   // "nuevo", then "viejo"
//     _medio()  { _lee() }                          // does not name `v`
//
// The register VM and the browser engine keep module state in one place and
// never had the question. It reached ZyBank as a TUI repaint bug — a notice
// painted, cleared, and painted again next turn from a store that never heard
// about the clearing — and was filed as irreducible after six minimal cases
// missed it, because every one of them called the reader directly.
<# ./zyb/estado_intermedia => e

e::correr()
